# OpenTrading — canonical AI engineering layer

Cursor rules here are intentionally thin. The source of truth is the vendor-neutral
layer under `.ai/` plus `docs/ai-engineering/`.

## Before working in this repo, read

- `.ai/README.md`
- `.ai/rules/architecture-invariants.md` (INV-1..INV-16 — non-negotiable)
- `.ai/rules/cross-review-rules.md`
- `.ai/context/repo-map.md` (PRE-00: docs only; no code yet)

## Working rules

- Route tasks via `docs/ai-engineering/ROUTING_RULES.md`: one primary specialist
  (`.ai/agents/`) + mandatory reviewers for the change class.
- Graphify first for codebase questions; run `graphify update .` after structural
  changes.
- Definition of Done: `.ai/rules/definition-of-done.md`; substantial work requires an
  adversarial Verification review (`.ai/workflows/verification-workflow.md`).
- Hard boundaries: LLMs propose, deterministic code decides capital (INV-1);
  point-in-time everywhere (INV-3); risk deterministic (INV-4); MT4 execution-only
  (INV-5).
- No orchestration frameworks (RuFlo, Claude Flow). No trading features during PRE-00.

## UI work

User-facing changes receive proportional UI review: existing tokens/components,
browser and axe checks. See `.ai/agents/command-center.md`.
